☠ MORTAL FRETS — The Fretboard Slayer
Retro arcade-style guitar fretboard training game inspired by Mortal Kombat. 8 game modes across Identification and Construction. Global leaderboard powered by Firebase.
🎮 Play Now

Game Modes
All modes: 10 questions per round · Score = errors (fewer = better) · Tiebreaker: time
Identification — see the question, press the correct button
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote IDDot on fretboard (frets 0–12, all strings)Press the correct note nameInterval IDR (root, red) + interval dot within ±3 frets/±2 stringsPress the correct interval (m2–P8)Chord IDReal voicing — triads on 3 adjacent strings, tetrads as Drop 2 / Drop 3 / Drop 2+4Press the correct chord typeScale IDFull scale in a 5-fret box, R = RootPress the correct scale name
Construction — target shown (illuminated button), build it, press SUBMIT
ModeWhat you seeWhat you doNote ConstructionTarget note illuminatedPlace ALL occurrences on the fretboardInterval ConstructionR pre-placed, interval illuminatedClick anywhere to place the note — auto-checks immediatelyChord ConstructionOne chord tone pre-placed (with role label), chord type illuminatedPlace remaining notes in any order, one per stringScale ConstructionR pre-placed in box, scale type illuminatedFill all scale positions in the box

Rules

Wrong answer (ID): stay on same question, retry. Timer keeps running.
Wrong SUBMIT (Construction): wrong dots → red, missing → orange. Click to fix, re-SUBMIT.
Mercy ☠: activates after 2 wrong answers. Hold to reveal full solution; release to retry. Resets each question.
Variety: same type appears at most twice per round; exact same question never repeats.
Box selection: Chord and Scale modes — fixed 5-fret box or 💀 KHAOS (random every question).
Notation: toggle A-B-C or Do-Re-Mi at any time.


Scoring
ErrorsResult0⚡ FLAWLESS VICTORY1–2EXCELLENT FIGHTER3–5SKILLED WARRIOR6–10FIGHT HARDER11–19FINISH HIM20+FATALITY

Music Theory Coverage
Notes: all 12 chromatic, frets 0–12, all 6 strings (standard tuning E A D G B e)
Intervals: m2 · M2 · m3 · M3 · P4 · TT · P5 · m6 · M6 · m7 · M7 · P8
Chords: Maj · min · Aug · Dim · Maj7 · Dom7 · min7 · ø7 · °7
Scales: Major · Natural Minor · Harmonic Minor · Melodic Minor · Whole-Half Dim · Half-Whole Dim
Chord voicings: triads on all 4 adjacent 3-string groups · Drop 2 on 3 adjacent 4-string groups · Drop 3 on 4 groups (2 standard + 2 non-standard) · Drop 2+4 on 2 groups · all inversions

Deploy on GitHub Pages

Upload mortal_frets.html renamed as index.html
Settings → Pages → branch main → / (root)
Live at https://yourusername.github.io/repo-name/


Global Leaderboard (Firebase)
Uses Firebase Realtime Database REST API — no SDK, direct HTTP calls, always reads fresh from server.
Setup:

console.firebase.google.com → new project → Realtime Database → Start in test mode
Copy the database URL (e.g. https://your-project-default-rtdb.europe-west1.firebasedatabase.app)
Replace FB_CONFIG near the top of the <script> tag with your project values
Set rules (Realtime Database → Rules):

json{
  "rules": {
    "leaderboards": {
      "$mode": {
        ".read": true,
        ".write": true
      }
    }
  }
}
Separate leaderboard per mode. Sorted by errors asc → time asc.

Tech Stack
Pure HTML/CSS/JavaScript · Web Audio API · SVG fretboard · Firebase REST API · Press Start 2P + Rajdhani · CRT scanlines · MK-style screen flash + shake
